{
  "title": "Namaz of Lady Fatimah al-Zahra (s.a.)",
  "data": "Two Units with the Litany\nPray 2 units. In the first unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) 100 times. In the second, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116).\nAfter the taslim, recite this litany:\nسُبْحَانَ ذِي الْعِزِّ الشَّامِخِ الْمُنِيْفِ\nSUBHAANA DHIL I'ZZISH SHAAMIKHIL MUNEEF\nGlory be to the Lord of Honor and Sublime Authority.\nسُبْحَانَ ذِي الْجَلَالِ الْبَاذِخِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nSUBHAANA DHIL JALAALIL BAADHIKHIL A'ZEEM\nGlory be to the Lord of Majesty and Exalted Greatness.\nسُبْحَانَ ذِي الْمُلْكِ الْفَاخِرِ الْقَدِيْمِ\nSUBHAANA DHIL MULKIL FAAKHIRIL QADEEM\nGlory be to the Lord of eternal, splendid sovereignty.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَبِسَ الْبَهْجَةَ وَالْجَمَالَ\nSUBHAANA MAN LABISAL BAHJATA WAL JAMAAL\nGlory be to Him Who dressed Himself with splendor and beauty.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ تَرَدَّى بِالنُّوْرِ وَالْوَقَارِ\nSUBHAANA MAN TARADDAA BIN NOORI WAL WAQAAR\nGlory be to Him Who is clad in light and dignity.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ يَرٰى اَثَرَ النَّمْلِ فِي الصَّفَا\nSUBHAANA MAN YARAA ATHARAN NAMLI FIS SAFAA\nGlory be to Him Who makes out the footprints of the ant on the stone.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ يَرٰى وَقْعَ الطَّيْرِ فِي الْهَوَاۤءِ\nSUBHAANA MAN YARAA WAQ'AT TAYRI FIL HAWAA'\nGlory be to Him Who knows (the exact time and place of) the bird dipping down through the air.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ هُوَ هٰكَذَا لَا هٰكَذَا غَيْرُهُ.\nSUBHAANA MAN HUWA HAAKADHAA LAA HAAKADHAA GHAYRUH\nGlory be to Him Who is like this and no one (other than Him) is like this.\nThen recite [Tasbeeh al-Zahra](I9) and invoke Allah's blessings upon the Holy Prophet and his Household.",
  "tabs": [
    "Shaykh al-Tusi's Form\nPray 2 units. In the first unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) 100 times. In the second, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) 100 times.\nAfter the taslim, recite [Tasbeeh al-Zahra](I9).\nThen uncover your knees and arms and prostrate, every part of prostration touching the ground with nothing in between.\nIn the prostration, pray for what you need, and recite:\nيَا مَنْ لَيْسَ غَيْرَهٗ رَبٌّ يُدْعٰى\nYAA MAN LAYSA GHAYRAHOO RABBUN YUD'AA\nO He besides Whom there is no lord to be supplicated!\nيَا مَنْ لَيْسَ فَوْقَهٗ اِلٰهٌ يُخْشٰى\nYAA MAN LAYSA FAWQAHOO ILAAHUN YUKHSHAA\nO He above Whom there is no god to be feared!\nيَا مَنْ لَيْسَ دُوْنَهٗ مَلِكٌ يُتَّقٰى\nYAA MAN LAYSA DOONAHOO MALIKUN YUTTAQAA\nO He except Whom there is no master to be revered!\nيَا مَنْ لَيْسَ لَهٗ وَزِيْرٌ يُّؤْتٰى\nYAA MAN LAYSA LAHOO WAZEERUN YU'TAA\nO He Who has no counselor to be approached!\nيَا مَنْ لَيْسَ لَهٗ حَاجِبٌ يُرْشٰى\nYAA MAN LAYSA LAHOO HAAJIBUN YURSHAA\nO He Who has no attendant to be bribed!\nيَا مَنْ لَيْسَ لَهٗ بَوَّابٌ يُغْشٰى\nYAA MAN LAYSA LAHOO BAWWAABUN YUGHSHAA\nO He Who has no doorkeeper to be visited (secretly)!\nيَا مَنْ لَا يَزْدَادُ عَلٰى كَثْرَةِ السُّؤَالِ اِلَّا كَرَمًا وَجُوْدًا وَعَلٰى كَثْرَةِ الذُّنُوْبِ اِلَّا عَفْوًا وَصَفْحًا\nYAA MAN LAA YAZDAADU A'LAA KATHRATIS SU'AALI ILLAA KARAMAN WA JOODAN WA A'LAA KATHRATIDH DHUNOOBI ILLAA A'FWAN WA SAFHAA\nO He Who gives not but generously and liberally no matter how many the demands are and deals not with numerous sins but mercifully and kindly!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ.\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nSend blessings upon Muhammad and his Household.\nThen mention your own needs.",
    "Four Units on Friday Morning\nOn Friday morning, do ghusl and pray 4 units, in sets of 2.\nIn the first unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) 50 times.\nIn the second, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-'Adiyat](A104) 50 times.\nIn the third, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Zalzalah](A103) 50 times.\nIn the fourth, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Nasr](A114) 50 times.\nAfter the prayer, recite:\nاِلٰهِيْ وَسَيِّدِيْ مَنْ تَهَيَّاَ اَوْ تَعَبّٰى اَوْ اَعَدَّ اَوِ اسْتَعَدَّ لِوِفَادَةِ مَخْلُوْقٍ\nILAAHEE WA SAYYIDEE MAN TAHAYYA'A AW TA'ABBAA AW A'ADDA AWIS TA'ADDA LIWIFAADATI MAKHLOOQ\nO My God and Master, whilst one prepares oneself, sets up, arranges, or gets ready for visiting a mortal\nرَجَاۤءَ رِفْدِهٖ وَفَوَاۤئِدِهٖ وَنَاۤئِلِهٖ وَفَوَاضِلِهٖ وَجَوَاۤئِزِهٖ\nRAJAA'A RIFDIHEE WA FAWAA'IDIHEE WA NAA'ILIHEE WA FAWAADILIHEE WA JAWAA'IZIH\nin the hope of attaining a gift, interests, a souvenir, bequests, or presents from him,\nفَاِلَيْكَ يَاۤ اِلٰهِيْ كَانَتْ تَهْيِئَتِيْ وَتَعْبِئَتِيْ وَاِعْدَادِيْ وَاسْتِعْدَادِيْ\nFA-ILAYKA YAA ILAAHEE KAANAT TAHYI'ATEE WA TA'BI'ATEE WA I'DAADEE WASTI'DAADEE\nto You, O my God, have I prepared myself, set up, arranged and got ready\nرَجَاۤءَ فَوَاۤئِدِكَ وَمَعْرُوْفِكَ وَنَاۤئِلِكَ وَجَوَاۤئِزِكَ\nRAJAA'A FAWAA'IDIKA WA MA'ROOFIKA WA NAA'ILIKA WA JAWAA'IZIK\nin the hope of attaining Your interests, favors, souvenirs, and presents.\nفَلَا تُخَيِّبْنِيْ مِنْ ذٰلِكَ\nFALAA TUKHAYYIBNEE MIN DHAALIK\nHence, (please) do not disappoint me of all these.\nيَا مَنْ لَّا تَخِيْبُ عَلَيْهِ مَسْاَلَةُ السَّاۤئِلِ وَلَا تَنْقُصُهٗ عَطِيَّةُ نَاۤئِلٍ\nYAA MAL LAA TAKHEEBU A'LAYHI MAS'ALATUS SAA'ILI WA LAA TANQUSUHOO A'TIYYATU NAA'IL\nO You with Whom no asker is disappointed and no present of an earner causes You reduction.\nفَاِنِّيْ لَمْ اٰتِكَ بِعَمَلٍ صَالِحٍ قَدَّمْتُهٗ\nFA-INNEE LAM AATIKA BI-A'MALIN SAALIHIN QADDAMTUH\nIn fact, I have not come to You with a righteous deed that I have done\nوَلَا شَفَاعَةِ مَخْلُوْقٍ رَجَوْتُهٗ اَتَقَرَّبُ اِلَيْكَ بِشَفَاعَتِهٖ\nWA LAA SHAFAA'ATI MAKHLOOQIN RAJAWTUHOO ATAQARRABU ILAYKA BISHAFAA'ATIH\nnor with an intercession of a creature that I hope to seek Your nearness through him\nاِلَّا مُحَمَّدًا وَاَهْلِ بَيْتِهٖ صَلَوَاتُكَ عَلَيْهِ وَعَلَيْهِمْ،\nILLAA MUHAMMADAN WA AHLI BAYTIHEE SALAWAATUKA A'LAYHI WA A'LAYHIM\nsave Muhammad and his Household, Your blessings be upon him and them.\nاَتَيْتُكَ اَرْجُوْ عَظِيْمَ عَفْوِكَ الَّذِيْ عُدْتَ بِهٖ عَلَى الْخَطَّاۤئِيْنَ عِنْدَ عُكُوْفِهِمْ عَلَى الْمَحَارِمِ\nATAYTUKA ARJOO A'ZEEMA A'FWIKAL LADHEE U'DTA BIHEE A'LAL KHATTAA'EENA I'NDA U'KOOFIHIM A'LAL MAHAARIM\nI am coming to You hoping for Your munificent amnesty that You have conferred upon the sinners who confined themselves to the commitment to forbidden acts;\nفَلَمْ يَمْنَعْكَ طُوْلُ عُكُوْفِهِمْ عَلَى الْمَحَارِمِ اَنْ جُدْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِالْمَغْفِرَةِ\nFALAM YAMNA'KA TOOLU U'KOOFIHIM A'LAL MAHAARIMI AN JUDTA A'LAYHIM BIL MAGHFIRAH\nnevertheless, their long-lasting commitment to forbidden acts has not made You stop conferring upon them with Your forgiveness.\nوَاَنْتَ سَيِّدِي الْعَوَّادُ بِالنَّعْمَاۤءِ وَاَنَا الْعَوَّادُ بِالْخَطَاۤءِ\nWA ANTA SAYYIDIL A'WWAADU BIN NA'MAA'I WA ANAL A'WWAADU BIL KHATAA'\nYou, O my Master, always confer upon me with Your graces while I always recommit sins.\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِحَقِّ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ اَنْ تَغْفِرَ لِيْ ذَنْبِيَ الْعَظِيْمَ\nAS'ALUKA BIHAQQI MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHIT TAAHIREENA AN TAGHFIRA LEE DHANBIYAL A'ZEEM\nI thus ask You by the Right of Muhammad and his Household, the Immaculate, to forgive my grand sins,\nفَاِنَّهٗ لَا يَغْفِرُ الْعَظِيْمَ اِلَّا الْعَظِيْمُ\nFA-INNAHOO LAA YAGHFIRUL A'ZEEMA ILLAL A'ZEEM\nfor none forgives the grand sins but the All-great.\nيَا عَظِيْمُ يَا عَظِيْمُ يَا عَظِيْمُ يَا عَظِيْمُ.\nYAA A'ZEEMU YAA A'ZEEMU YAA A'ZEEMU YAA A'ZEEM\nO All-great, O All-great, O All-great, O All-great."
  ],
  "merits": "Two Units with the Litany: It is narrated that Lady Fatimah al-Zahra' (s.a.) used to offer a two-unit prayer taught by Archangel Gabriel, and would say this litany after the taslim. Sayyid Ibn Tawus adds that it is better to say the famous [Tasbeeh al-Zahra](I9) after offering this prayer and then invoke Almighty Allah's blessings upon the Holy Prophet and his Household.\n\nShaykh al-Tusi's Form: In Misbah al-Mutahajjid, Shaykh al-Tusi has recorded that Lady Fatimah al-Zahra's prayer is offered in this way.\n\nFour Units on Friday Morning: Shaykh al-Tusi and Sayyid Ibn Tawus have reported on the authority of Safwan that Muhammad ibn Ali al-Halabi, once, visited Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) one Friday and asked him to teach him the best deed to be practiced on Fridays. The Imam (a.s.) said: Listen, Muhammad! I do not know anyone who was more beloved and more respected than Lady Fatimah al-Zahra' (s.a.) in the view of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.). Likewise, I do not know anything that was more valuable than that which he had taught her to do on Fridays. [Surah al-Nasr](A114) was the concluding revelation."
